1
00:01:38,250 --> 00:01:43,870
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:46,740
[Episode 4]

3
00:01:47,150 --> 00:01:48,070
Does it hurt?

4
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:51,920
You're not the doctor from earlier.

5
00:01:55,310 --> 00:01:56,120
Oh, it's you.

6
00:01:56,710 --> 00:01:57,640
You know me?

7
00:01:59,789 --> 00:02:01,430
That day, your brother and I

8
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:02,900
[Emergency]

9
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:03,100
were at the No. 1 Hospital.

10
00:02:04,310 --> 00:02:05,280
I remember now.

11
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:06,560
The one who fought with Zhengguang.

12
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:08,160
We were just playing around.

13
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:09,080
Give it to me.

14
00:02:11,870 --> 00:02:12,680
Your white blood cell count

15
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:13,710
is normal,

16
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:15,560
but the neutrophil percentage

17
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:16,870
has increased.

18
00:02:18,030 --> 00:02:19,310
Platelets are at 50.

19
00:02:20,710 --> 00:02:21,870
Come, lie down on the bed back there.

20
00:02:21,870 --> 00:02:23,000
I'll examine you.

21
00:02:23,150 --> 00:02:23,880
Come on, Mom.

22
00:02:24,750 --> 00:02:25,470
Get up.

23
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:27,079
Let's go.

24
00:02:30,310 --> 00:02:31,240
If it hurts later,

25
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:31,970
just tell me.

26
00:02:39,430 --> 00:02:40,630
It doesn't hurt here.

27
00:02:44,079 --> 00:02:45,280
It hurts a lot here.

28
00:02:46,590 --> 00:02:47,470
Alright, we're done.

29
00:02:47,470 --> 00:02:48,240
Get up.

30
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:49,000
Come on, Mom.

31
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,710
You'll have an ultrasound in a bit.

32
00:02:50,710 --> 00:02:52,470
Why an ultrasound?

33
00:02:52,750 --> 00:02:54,120
Where's the doctor from earlier?

34
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:56,050
He hid because he was afraid of you.

35
00:02:57,030 --> 00:02:58,630
Then just give me an IV drip.

36
00:02:58,630 --> 00:03:00,310
Anyone can do it, really.

37
00:03:00,750 --> 00:03:02,120
I can't give you an IV drip.

38
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:03,310
Our preliminary diagnosis is

39
00:03:03,310 --> 00:03:04,560
that you most likely have

40
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:05,680
ureteral stones

41
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:07,630
accompanied by hydronephrosis
and infection.

42
00:03:07,630 --> 00:03:09,560
So you must do an ultrasound first.

43
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:11,360
We'll diagnose further

44
00:03:11,430 --> 00:03:12,120
and then decide

45
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:14,050
on your follow-up treatment plan.

46
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:21,040
[No smoking]

47
00:03:16,150 --> 00:03:18,000
You make me do one test first,

48
00:03:18,870 --> 00:03:20,750
then trick me into doing another.

49
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:24,660
[Emergency Room 18]

50
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,060
You guys are just taking all my money.

51
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:28,120
The money you pay for treatment
doesn't go to me.

52
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:29,430
Why would I trick you?

53
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:39,410
Come on, take your mom there right now.

54
00:03:39,470 --> 00:03:39,960
She already

55
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:41,120
has chills and a fever.

56
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:42,800
Although her white blood cell count
is normal,

57
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:44,079
her neutrophils

58
00:03:44,079 --> 00:03:45,750
have clearly changed.

59
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:47,190
Her platelets are so low,

60
00:03:47,190 --> 00:03:48,910
she's very likely
to have a severe infection

61
00:03:48,910 --> 00:03:50,120
and develop sepsis.

62
00:03:50,430 --> 00:03:51,840
If delayed for too long,

63
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:53,280
the patient will go into shock

64
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:55,010
and even face the risk of death.

65
00:03:55,430 --> 00:03:56,190
Okay.

66
00:03:56,190 --> 00:03:56,910
Let's go.

67
00:03:56,910 --> 00:03:57,800
Wait,

68
00:03:58,079 --> 00:04:00,190
I haven't even agreed to do it yet.

69
00:04:00,190 --> 00:04:02,470
Why did you just write the orders for me?

70
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:04,540
What if after the test,

71
00:04:04,910 --> 00:04:06,870
I don't have stones?

72
00:04:07,750 --> 00:04:08,910
Can I get a refund?

73
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:10,000
No refunds.

74
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,400
Then I won't do it.

75
00:04:12,150 --> 00:04:14,150
Who knows if you're actually right?

76
00:04:14,430 --> 00:04:14,960
Okay.

77
00:04:15,840 --> 00:04:16,560
Anyway, I've said

78
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:17,690
what I needed to say.

79
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:19,320
If you don't want to do it,

80
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:21,070
just throw these orders in the trash.

81
00:04:21,070 --> 00:04:22,480
We'll do it. We'll do it.

82
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,480
Mom, I know this doctor.

83
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:26,270
He came back from a big hospital
in the South.

84
00:04:26,270 --> 00:04:27,130
He's very good.

85
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:29,070
He specializes in brain surgery.

86
00:04:29,070 --> 00:04:30,040
He's an authority.

87
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:31,070
It's fine to do what he says.

88
00:04:31,070 --> 00:04:32,400
Let's do an ultrasound.

89
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:34,840
From a big hospital in the South?

90
00:04:34,950 --> 00:04:36,040
Then why did he come back?

91
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:38,100
My mom died. I'm here for the funeral.

92
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:39,370
That's not allowed?

93
00:04:44,070 --> 00:04:45,360
You've got some nerve.

94
00:04:47,190 --> 00:04:48,040
Let's do it.

95
00:04:48,270 --> 00:04:49,070
Let's do it.

96
00:04:49,950 --> 00:04:50,720
Do it, do it, do it.

97
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:51,360
Okay.

98
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:54,380
Thank you, doctor. Thank you.

99
00:05:01,610 --> 00:05:04,390
[Emergency]

100
00:05:02,830 --> 00:05:03,890
Does it still hurt?

101
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:04,830
It's okay.

102
00:05:04,420 --> 00:05:05,940
[Quiet]

103
00:05:04,830 --> 00:05:06,360
It hurts in waves.

104
00:05:06,580 --> 00:05:10,070
[Quiet] [Red zone]

105
00:05:07,750 --> 00:05:08,830
It's so annoying.

106
00:05:09,070 --> 00:05:10,270
We have to cooperate.

107
00:05:11,270 --> 00:05:12,070
Come on.

108
00:05:17,610 --> 00:05:21,730
[Xiaoximen Hospital
Ultrasonic Examination Report]

109
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:19,680
This stone of yours

110
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:21,830
is blocking the lower part
of your right ureter.

111
00:05:21,830 --> 00:05:23,090
It's 1.8 centimeters.

112
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:25,430
And your right kidney

113
00:05:25,750 --> 00:05:27,410
has obvious hydronephrosis.

114
00:05:28,750 --> 00:05:29,720
Is it serious?

115
00:05:30,310 --> 00:05:32,000
When I felt uncomfortable before,

116
00:05:31,830 --> 00:05:35,659
[Chest Pain and Stroke]

117
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:34,600
I used my cupped hands
to pat my lower back,

118
00:05:34,830 --> 00:05:36,159
and it felt much better.

119
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:37,510
Good palm strength.

120
00:05:37,510 --> 00:05:39,750
You patted the stone
right into the ureter.

121
00:05:39,750 --> 00:05:40,190
Alright.

122
00:05:40,190 --> 00:05:41,770
You can go to the urology department now.

123
00:05:41,770 --> 00:05:48,970
[Chest Pain and Stroke]

124
00:05:42,190 --> 00:05:42,600
Okay.

125
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:44,240
I spent money here,

126
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:45,560
and you're sending me

127
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:46,830
somewhere else.

128
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:48,630
Didn't I waste my money?

129
00:05:48,630 --> 00:05:50,310
I'm only responsible for the diagnosis.

130
00:05:50,310 --> 00:05:51,480
The specific treatment

131
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:53,000
has to be done by a specialist doctor.

132
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,060
-Yeah.
-Whatever.

133
00:05:54,510 --> 00:05:55,430
I came to you,

134
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:58,130
so you have to be responsible for me
to the end.

135
00:05:58,630 --> 00:05:59,480
That can't be done here.

136
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:01,080
Then I'll complain about you

137
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:04,820
and make you lose your job.

138
00:06:05,480 --> 00:06:06,600
I know

139
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:08,070
President Long here.

140
00:06:08,070 --> 00:06:09,160
That's great!

141
00:06:09,750 --> 00:06:10,920
You go right now

142
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:12,780
and have him fire me immediately.

143
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:31,160
Come on.

144
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:32,040
Take your mom immediately

145
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:32,950
to the urology department
to find a doctor.

146
00:06:32,950 --> 00:06:35,360
-Okay.
-Get the admission procedures handled.

147
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:36,159
Don't worry.

148
00:06:36,159 --> 00:06:37,890
It won't delay your complaint.

149
00:06:40,159 --> 00:06:41,690
Came back from the South...

150
00:06:42,510 --> 00:06:44,630
So doctors who came back
from big hospitals in the South

151
00:06:44,630 --> 00:06:46,270
talk tougher

152
00:06:46,270 --> 00:06:47,530
than the doctors here.

153
00:06:50,430 --> 00:06:52,270
Let's go get you admitted first.

154
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:55,750
Doctor.

155
00:06:57,680 --> 00:07:00,210
You came back from a big hospital
in the South,

156
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:02,510
so you must have graduated

157
00:07:02,510 --> 00:07:04,270
from a prestigious university, right?

158
00:07:04,270 --> 00:07:06,070
You must be very educated.

159
00:07:07,070 --> 00:07:07,750
Come on.

160
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:10,190
Help me take a look at this.

161
00:07:11,950 --> 00:07:13,190
This draft...

162
00:07:13,190 --> 00:07:15,040
Can you help me polish it?

163
00:07:15,870 --> 00:07:17,000
Thank you.

164
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:22,400
Sorry to trouble you. Thank you.

165
00:07:27,030 --> 00:07:27,500
[Fighting for justice]

166
00:07:27,520 --> 00:07:27,890
[Li Changlu, former director of the former
Fucheng Paper Mill, is utterly heartless]

167
00:07:27,920 --> 00:07:28,300
[He sold the paper factory at a low price
and embezzled national assets]

168
00:07:28,330 --> 00:07:29,080
[Causing more than 100 workers
to lose their jobs]

169
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:29,840
[They've been defending their rights
for 25 years]

170
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:30,580
[But the matter
still has no proper resolution]

171
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:31,700
[And Li Changlu ran away with the money]

172
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:32,980
[Duan Yinghua, former workshop director
of the paper mill]

173
00:07:47,070 --> 00:07:49,710
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

174
00:07:47,630 --> 00:07:48,120
Bro.

175
00:08:06,240 --> 00:08:07,920
Crappy place,
crappy hospital, crappy door!

176
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:09,750
Damn it, what the hell?

177
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:11,050
What is he doing?

178
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:14,630
What's going on? What did he say?

179
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:17,060
Histrionic personality.

180
00:08:17,390 --> 00:08:18,310
Just like you.

181
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:20,430
Screw off!

182
00:08:32,110 --> 00:08:32,870
Hello.

183
00:08:33,669 --> 00:08:35,750
How does it feel to just start working?

184
00:08:34,130 --> 00:08:37,820
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

185
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:39,120
Weirdos.

186
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:39,960
Weirdos?

187
00:08:40,270 --> 00:08:42,789
Are you talking about the patients
or the doctors?

188
00:08:42,789 --> 00:08:44,320
Bro, you're scheduled
for the night shift tomorrow.

189
00:08:44,320 --> 00:08:45,720
Don't forget, 4 o'clock.

190
00:08:47,670 --> 00:08:48,870
They're all weirdos.

191
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:50,510
I've never seen a hospital like this.

192
00:08:50,510 --> 00:08:52,370
If it weren't for President Long,

193
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:54,750
this hospital would have been shut down
long ago.

194
00:08:54,750 --> 00:08:56,080
It's just a matter of time.

195
00:08:56,080 --> 00:08:57,810
There are hardly any patients.

196
00:08:58,360 --> 00:08:59,870
That's right.

197
00:09:00,630 --> 00:09:02,440
This hospital is closest
to the crematorium.

198
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:02,910
Look,

199
00:09:02,910 --> 00:09:05,200
it's in the suburbs
and the medical conditions are poor.

200
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:05,960
Isn't there

201
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:07,390
a rhyme like this?

202
00:09:07,630 --> 00:09:09,510
Xiaoximen Hospital faces west,

203
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:12,320
a fast track to heaven.

204
00:09:12,630 --> 00:09:15,030
Who in their right mind
would go to heaven to see a doctor?

205
00:09:15,030 --> 00:09:15,830
Can you not go?

206
00:09:16,030 --> 00:09:17,230
What do you want to do?

207
00:09:17,550 --> 00:09:18,870
Is there anything wrong with me
wanting to make money?

208
00:09:18,870 --> 00:09:19,630
I don't want to spend my whole life

209
00:09:19,630 --> 00:09:20,790
being a loser here, is that wrong?

210
00:09:20,790 --> 00:09:22,030
What's wrong with our place?

211
00:09:22,030 --> 00:09:22,750
The doctor from the big city

212
00:09:22,750 --> 00:09:24,150
came back too, didn't he?

213
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:25,510
That's because he couldn't compete
with the better ones,

214
00:09:25,510 --> 00:09:26,150
isn't it?

215
00:09:26,150 --> 00:09:26,750
Step aside!

216
00:09:26,750 --> 00:09:28,120
You'll make money off anything, huh?

217
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:28,720
What's wrong with that?

218
00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:30,870
What the hell kind of doctors
are in this hospital?

219
00:09:30,870 --> 00:09:32,200
They're all incompetent,

220
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:33,400
just coasting along.

221
00:09:34,150 --> 00:09:35,840
Isn't it responsible
for its own profits and losses?

222
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:37,390
It hasn't lost enough yet.

223
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:42,000
Then I hope it goes bankrupt tomorrow.

224
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,840
How's that lying flat
and doing nothing method

225
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:45,240
I taught you working out?

226
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:46,750
Don't mention it. I used it,

227
00:09:46,750 --> 00:09:47,810
but it didn't work.

228
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:50,130
Then you're not lying flat enough yet.

229
00:09:50,550 --> 00:09:51,630
What do you mean not flat enough?

230
00:09:51,630 --> 00:09:52,390
I lie flat,

231
00:09:52,390 --> 00:09:54,030
but they lie even flatter than me.

232
00:09:54,030 --> 00:09:55,080
If I'm the Sanjiang Plain,

233
00:09:54,870 --> 00:09:59,940
[Entrance]

234
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:56,600
they're the Qaidam Basin.

235
00:09:56,670 --> 00:09:57,720
The method you taught me

236
00:09:57,720 --> 00:09:58,870
almost made me blend in with them

237
00:09:58,870 --> 00:10:00,360
as fast as possible, you know?

238
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:02,510
What a crappy method. Stop messing around.

239
00:10:02,510 --> 00:10:04,120
Qaidam Basin, huh?

240
00:10:04,390 --> 00:10:04,960
Tell me,

241
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:06,890
how much of a basin have you become?

242
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:12,630
What are you doing?

243
00:10:12,630 --> 00:10:13,320
No.

244
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:13,550
Security.

245
00:10:13,550 --> 00:10:14,790
What are you doing?

246
00:10:14,790 --> 00:10:15,670
Didn't I tell you

247
00:10:15,670 --> 00:10:17,000
Dr. Liu is off work?

248
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:18,720
See for yourself.

249
00:10:19,270 --> 00:10:19,910
She...

250
00:10:21,670 --> 00:10:23,330
What's going on with you guys?

251
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:25,120
You told me to go
to the urology department, right?

252
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:26,150
Urology won't treat her,

253
00:10:26,150 --> 00:10:27,150
so who else am I supposed to turn to?

254
00:10:27,150 --> 00:10:28,360
Why won't they treat you?

255
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:29,750
He said he didn't dare to treat it.

256
00:10:29,750 --> 00:10:31,550
What kind of thing is that to say?

257
00:10:31,870 --> 00:10:33,270
Put me through to urology.

258
00:10:33,270 --> 00:10:33,910
I'm looking for the doctor

259
00:10:33,910 --> 00:10:35,840
who was treating Ms. Duan earlier.

260
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:37,200
Dr. Liu.

261
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:40,630
Hello.

262
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:43,030
This is Liu Zhengliang from
the emergency surgery department.

263
00:10:43,030 --> 00:10:44,030
I want to know

264
00:10:44,030 --> 00:10:44,630
why didn't you

265
00:10:44,630 --> 00:10:46,150
operate on Ms. Duan?

266
00:10:46,550 --> 00:10:47,790
The patient has a co-infection.

267
00:10:47,790 --> 00:10:49,550
It's that serious.
How are we supposed to operate?

268
00:10:49,550 --> 00:10:51,030
You can insert a ureteral stent
to drain it.

269
00:10:51,030 --> 00:10:52,440
Our director left for a job

270
00:10:52,440 --> 00:10:53,840
at a hospital down south.

271
00:10:54,240 --> 00:10:55,360
Don't you have any other doctors here

272
00:10:55,360 --> 00:10:56,120
who can perform the procedure?

273
00:10:56,120 --> 00:10:57,600
I don't have the skills.

274
00:10:57,960 --> 00:10:59,720
The others are even less qualified
than I am.

275
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:01,720
If her infection worsens

276
00:11:02,030 --> 00:11:03,840
during the operation,

277
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:05,240
causing an accident,

278
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:06,360
I can't take responsibility for that.

279
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:07,240
If she

280
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:08,300
isn't treated now,

281
00:11:08,360 --> 00:11:09,910
her infection will get worse and worse.

282
00:11:09,910 --> 00:11:11,080
If she develops

283
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:12,000
septic shock later,

284
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:13,320
the mortality rate is very high.

285
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:15,120
I've told the old lady.

286
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:15,790
You'd better

287
00:11:15,790 --> 00:11:17,390
go to a higher-level hospital.

288
00:11:17,390 --> 00:11:18,240
You know what?

289
00:11:18,390 --> 00:11:19,080
Her son

290
00:11:19,080 --> 00:11:20,080
almost grabbed me by the collar

291
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:21,150
and beat me up.

292
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:23,200
This mother and son are too unreasonable.

293
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:23,840
Look,

294
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:25,840
if things get out of hand,
just call security.

295
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:26,840
Our security guard, Li,

296
00:11:26,840 --> 00:11:27,600
has trained in

297
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:29,460
Tiger and Leopard-style kung fu.

298
00:11:31,390 --> 00:11:32,270
What did he say?

299
00:11:35,360 --> 00:11:35,960
Mom.

300
00:11:35,960 --> 00:11:36,480
Auntie,

301
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:37,390
the doctor in the urology department

302
00:11:37,390 --> 00:11:38,320
didn't lie to you.

303
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:39,360
Your infection is very serious.

304
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:40,360
You need surgery.

305
00:11:40,630 --> 00:11:41,830
I won't have surgery.

306
00:11:42,270 --> 00:11:44,550
I have a lot of things to do.

307
00:11:44,550 --> 00:11:46,950
-I don't have time.
-What are you busy with?

308
00:11:48,840 --> 00:11:49,750
The big character poster...

309
00:11:49,160 --> 00:11:53,830
[Patient Satisfaction Survey]

310
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:50,600
Look,

311
00:11:51,390 --> 00:11:52,870
all the idioms on this poster are wrong.

312
00:11:52,870 --> 00:11:54,270
No one can understand it.

313
00:11:56,670 --> 00:11:59,030
I was wondering
why no one paid attention to me.

314
00:11:58,950 --> 00:12:00,140
[Li Changlu sold the paper mill for a fraction
of its value and embezzled state assets]

315
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:01,790
It turns out it was written incorrectly.

316
00:12:00,170 --> 00:12:00,970
[leaving over 100 workers out of a job.]

317
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:01,970
[25 years of fighting for justice,
and still no resolution.]

318
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:02,830
[Meanwhile, Li Changlu fled
with the money.]

319
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,670
After so many years,

320
00:12:07,510 --> 00:12:09,000
this is the first time

321
00:12:09,360 --> 00:12:11,960
anyone's paid attention
to what I've written.

322
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:13,790
Let me tell you,

323
00:12:13,910 --> 00:12:15,630
your mother's infection is very serious.

324
00:12:15,630 --> 00:12:17,320
She needs surgery as soon as possible.

325
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:19,000
But the urologist here

326
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:19,870
doesn't feel confident treating it.

327
00:12:19,870 --> 00:12:21,320
-Where can she get treatment?
-I suggest you

328
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:22,670
go to a higher-level hospital.

329
00:12:22,670 --> 00:12:23,910
I don't have money.

330
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:25,240
To be honest,

331
00:12:26,270 --> 00:12:26,960
I don't want

332
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:29,000
to spend so much money
on medical treatment.

333
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,720
Come on, you keep saying no to everything.

334
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:32,360
This was originally a minor problem.

335
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:33,600
If you put it off for three to five days,

336
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:34,240
it could cost you your life.

337
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:35,440
So be it.

338
00:12:36,080 --> 00:12:37,200
In this life,

339
00:12:38,790 --> 00:12:41,270
I've encountered too many terrible things.

340
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:44,150
I've had enough of life.

341
00:12:44,150 --> 00:12:44,960
Mom.

342
00:12:48,510 --> 00:12:49,320
Dr. Liu.

343
00:12:50,120 --> 00:12:51,550
I can tell

344
00:12:52,200 --> 00:12:53,750
you're blunt,

345
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:56,000
but you've got a good heart.

346
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:02,720
I was just speaking out of anger.

347
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:06,750
If I can stay alive,
why would I want to die?

348
00:13:08,510 --> 00:13:09,790
But I only have

349
00:13:09,790 --> 00:13:11,600
1000 yuan in my pocket.

350
00:13:12,150 --> 00:13:13,550
Please help me

351
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:16,320
find a cheaper way to get treated.

352
00:13:16,320 --> 00:13:17,120
A thousand?

353
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:19,870
I'm putting my life

354
00:13:19,870 --> 00:13:21,600
in your hands.

355
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:22,750
I'm begging you.

356
00:13:22,750 --> 00:13:23,670
I'm really begging you.

357
00:13:23,670 --> 00:13:24,030
Don't...

358
00:13:24,030 --> 00:13:25,600
-Mom, what are you doing?
-Don't do this.

359
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:26,960
This is emotional blackmail.

360
00:13:26,960 --> 00:13:28,030
Dr. Liu,

361
00:13:28,030 --> 00:13:29,870
how's your first day of work?

362
00:13:30,390 --> 00:13:31,600
Long.

363
00:13:34,390 --> 00:13:35,670
Director Duan is here.

364
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:37,120
I'm going to die.

365
00:13:37,630 --> 00:13:39,480
I won't bother you anymore.

366
00:13:42,910 --> 00:13:44,480
I can't handle this person.

367
00:13:44,190 --> 00:13:50,090
[Clean Area]

368
00:13:44,870 --> 00:13:46,200
Get someone else to take over.

369
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:47,080
If you can't handle her,

370
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:48,550
why did you talk to her
about the big-character poster?

371
00:13:48,550 --> 00:13:50,030
I have OCD.

372
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:51,850
I can't stand seeing mistakes.

373
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:54,360
She's clinging to you now.

374
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:56,220
There's nothing I can do about it.

375
00:13:58,600 --> 00:13:59,910
Anyway, if you ask me,

376
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:01,720
she needs surgery

377
00:14:02,150 --> 00:14:03,790
and needs to go to a bigger hospital.

378
00:14:03,790 --> 00:14:05,630
Why go to a higher-level hospital?

379
00:14:05,630 --> 00:14:07,760
I know someone at Xiaoximen Hospital.

380
00:14:09,360 --> 00:14:10,080
Okay.

381
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:12,370
As long as you know someone.

382
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:13,840
Hey.

383
00:14:13,760 --> 00:14:16,840
[Clean Area]

384
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:16,320
Do you think this surgery is difficult?

385
00:14:23,250 --> 00:14:29,150
[Wound Debridement Room]
[Allergies]

386
00:14:34,720 --> 00:14:35,870
The patient's stone

387
00:14:36,270 --> 00:14:38,790
is currently stuck in the right ureter,

388
00:14:39,630 --> 00:14:40,720
right about here.

389
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:45,600
The urine is backing up
above the obstruction.

390
00:14:45,630 --> 00:14:46,630
There is already

391
00:14:46,630 --> 00:14:47,790
a co-infection.

392
00:14:47,960 --> 00:14:48,870
If we don't immediately

393
00:14:48,870 --> 00:14:49,790
drain the fluid

394
00:14:49,530 --> 00:14:54,880
[Supply Room]

395
00:14:49,790 --> 00:14:50,870
from above,

396
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:53,870
bacteria will continuously

397
00:14:53,870 --> 00:14:55,080
enter the bloodstream,

398
00:14:55,080 --> 00:14:56,840
which can easily cause sepsis

399
00:14:56,840 --> 00:14:59,080
or even septic shock.

400
00:14:59,720 --> 00:15:00,550
Considering

401
00:15:00,550 --> 00:15:02,550
the patient's current financial situation,

402
00:15:02,550 --> 00:15:03,790
the optimal plan

403
00:15:03,910 --> 00:15:07,390
is to place a ureteral stent to relieve
the obstruction and drain the urine.

404
00:15:07,390 --> 00:15:08,720
What does that involve?

405
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:10,420
Walk me through it.

406
00:15:13,240 --> 00:15:15,700
After the ureteroscope enters the bladder,

407
00:15:16,070 --> 00:15:17,670
we find the ureteral orifice

408
00:15:18,030 --> 00:15:19,550
insert a guidewire

409
00:15:20,030 --> 00:15:22,440
through the narrow space

410
00:15:22,440 --> 00:15:23,640
alongside the stone.

411
00:15:23,910 --> 00:15:26,080
Finally, we pass a stent

412
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:27,550
over the guidewire

413
00:15:27,550 --> 00:15:29,080
and into the ureter.

414
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:33,750
It's like

415
00:15:33,750 --> 00:15:35,080
a big rock blocking

416
00:15:35,240 --> 00:15:37,000
a road we normally take.

417
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:39,120
We need to find a way

418
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:40,550
around the rock to make a path

419
00:15:40,550 --> 00:15:42,390
to drain the fluid inside.

420
00:15:43,360 --> 00:15:44,080
That's it.

421
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:46,080
This kind of surgery

422
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:48,740
is usually performed
under spinal anesthesia.

423
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:50,840
The patient's platelet count is low,

424
00:15:50,840 --> 00:15:52,390
so spinal anesthesia could be risky.

425
00:15:52,390 --> 00:15:53,840
We'll have to use general anesthesia.

426
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:54,640
You know that.

427
00:15:56,270 --> 00:15:57,910
I understand once you elaborate.

428
00:15:57,910 --> 00:15:59,200
But the problem now is,

429
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:01,390
general anesthesia alone costs over 3,000.

430
00:16:01,390 --> 00:16:02,440
You go tell her.

431
00:16:02,870 --> 00:16:04,720
It doesn't matter who tells her about it.

432
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:06,000
The condition itself isn't hard to treat.

433
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:07,200
The real problem is
that she can't afford it.

434
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:08,150
Not even 3,000?

435
00:16:08,150 --> 00:16:08,720
Yes.

436
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:10,440
She'd rather wait to die at home

437
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:12,480
than spend so much money on treatment.

438
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:13,600
I can't believe anyone

439
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:14,440
would put that little money

440
00:16:14,440 --> 00:16:15,910
ahead of their own life.

441
00:16:16,070 --> 00:16:17,390
You don't understand
because you haven't been poor.

442
00:16:17,390 --> 00:16:18,270
Have you ever been poor?

443
00:16:18,270 --> 00:16:19,510
Who says I haven't been poor?

444
00:16:19,510 --> 00:16:20,630
I'm even worse off than she is right now.

445
00:16:20,630 --> 00:16:21,630
All my belongings combined

446
00:16:21,630 --> 00:16:22,630
are only worth about a thousand.

447
00:16:22,630 --> 00:16:24,030
You're young. You have time,

448
00:16:24,030 --> 00:16:25,670
skills, and knowledge.

449
00:16:25,670 --> 00:16:27,200
In that sense, you're rich.

450
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:28,630
Being poor isn't just about

451
00:16:28,630 --> 00:16:30,560
how much money you have in the bank.

452
00:16:36,080 --> 00:16:36,670
Is there

453
00:16:36,670 --> 00:16:38,070
a more money-saving way?

454
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:44,270
No. Find someone else.

455
00:16:45,790 --> 00:16:47,480
I thought you actually had some skills,

456
00:16:47,480 --> 00:16:48,630
some way to fix this.

457
00:16:51,390 --> 00:16:52,750
Of course I have a way.

458
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:54,150
I'm just afraid

459
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:55,840
that doctor wouldn't dare to use it.

460
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:57,000
I have a way, too.

461
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:57,840
I'm just afraid that doctor

462
00:16:57,840 --> 00:16:59,100
wouldn't dare to do it.

463
00:17:05,440 --> 00:17:06,960
Topical anesthesia.

464
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:11,880
This really depends on the doctor's feel
for the procedure.

465
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:12,790
And the surgery

466
00:17:12,790 --> 00:17:14,250
also has a risk of failure.

467
00:17:15,349 --> 00:17:16,069
How about this.

468
00:17:16,069 --> 00:17:17,240
I'll call the OR

469
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:18,790
and have them prepare

470
00:17:18,790 --> 00:17:20,119
a tube of lidocaine gel.

471
00:17:20,270 --> 00:17:21,730
I'll leave the rest to you.

472
00:17:21,750 --> 00:17:23,000
Why leave it to me?

473
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:24,790
Don't you know a doctor
at Xiaoximen Hospital?

474
00:17:24,790 --> 00:17:26,480
Weren't you a doctor
at Xiaoximen Hospital?

475
00:17:26,480 --> 00:17:28,400
Can you stop scheming against me?

476
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:30,240
I came prepared this time.

477
00:17:30,790 --> 00:17:32,400
I looked into your background.

478
00:17:32,400 --> 00:17:34,110
You used to work in urology.

479
00:17:34,110 --> 00:17:35,830
The patient's condition is critical now.

480
00:17:35,830 --> 00:17:37,960
I'll have the hospital's
on-call medical administrator

481
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:40,220
authorize you to perform the procedure.

482
00:17:45,310 --> 00:17:47,880
Is Duan your friend?

483
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:51,510
If the surgery is successful,

484
00:17:51,510 --> 00:17:52,480
can you let me go?

485
00:17:54,590 --> 00:17:56,120
First, she's not my friend.

486
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:57,400
She's just a patient.

487
00:17:57,590 --> 00:17:58,240
Second,

488
00:17:58,270 --> 00:18:00,200
don't use a patient's care
as a bargaining chip next time,

489
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:01,400
or I'll beat your ass.

490
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:09,010
[Surgery in Progress]

491
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:14,200
Can I see Dr. Liu

492
00:18:14,880 --> 00:18:17,270
during the surgery later?

493
00:18:17,270 --> 00:18:18,350
He's here, Auntie.

494
00:18:18,750 --> 00:18:19,640
Dr. Liu is here.

495
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:20,640
Let me adjust it for you.

496
00:18:20,640 --> 00:18:21,750
Take a look.

497
00:18:22,270 --> 00:18:23,550
Can you see him from here?

498
00:18:23,550 --> 00:18:26,240
I can't see. It's blurry.

499
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:27,160
I'm right here.

500
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:29,480
Don't worry. Don't be nervous.

501
00:18:29,480 --> 00:18:30,480
During the surgery,

502
00:18:30,480 --> 00:18:31,750
if you have any problems

503
00:18:31,750 --> 00:18:33,000
or feel any discomfort,

504
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:34,030
tell me directly.

505
00:18:36,110 --> 00:18:37,510
Just knowing you're here

506
00:18:38,550 --> 00:18:41,790
puts my mind at ease.

507
00:18:42,960 --> 00:18:44,560
The surgery will start soon.

508
00:18:44,590 --> 00:18:45,590
Don't be nervous.

509
00:18:56,960 --> 00:18:58,400
Found the ureteral orifice.

510
00:18:58,400 --> 00:18:59,060
Guidewire.

511
00:19:08,920 --> 00:19:10,550
The guidewire has passed the stone.

512
00:19:10,550 --> 00:19:11,720
Open the stent tube.

513
00:19:11,720 --> 00:19:12,400
Okay.

514
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:20,800
Let me briefly walk you
through the procedure.

515
00:19:23,350 --> 00:19:24,270
The simplest

516
00:19:24,270 --> 00:19:25,510
and cheapest method

517
00:19:25,510 --> 00:19:27,400
is topical anesthesia

518
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:28,800
under local anesthesia.

519
00:19:30,070 --> 00:19:31,440
This surgery really

520
00:19:31,750 --> 00:19:33,810
depends on the surgeon's feel for it.

521
00:19:34,350 --> 00:19:37,210
So there's still some risk
involved in the surgery.

522
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:38,160
It's fine.

523
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:39,820
My mom and I both trust Dr. Liu.

524
00:19:43,030 --> 00:19:44,110
Even with this

525
00:19:44,110 --> 00:19:45,440
simplest approach,

526
00:19:45,960 --> 00:19:48,020
1,000 yuan is definitely not enough.

527
00:19:48,480 --> 00:19:50,070
The anesthetic costs a dozen yuan.

528
00:19:50,070 --> 00:19:52,720
With the procedure, post-op monitoring,
and hospital stay,

529
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:54,550
she'll need at least
five days in the hospital.

530
00:19:54,550 --> 00:19:55,400
I think

531
00:19:55,960 --> 00:19:57,420
it'll cost at least 5,000.

532
00:19:57,720 --> 00:19:58,750
Dabao, we're at the hospital.

533
00:19:58,750 --> 00:20:00,030
Come in.

534
00:20:00,030 --> 00:20:00,960
Come in.

535
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:01,720
Come in.

536
00:20:02,590 --> 00:20:03,440
Don't stop me.

537
00:20:03,440 --> 00:20:04,310
I'm looking for a doctor.

538
00:20:04,310 --> 00:20:05,200
Doctor!

539
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:05,730
Don't...

540
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:06,680
Don't stop me.

541
00:20:06,680 --> 00:20:07,720
Why are you stopping me?

542
00:20:07,720 --> 00:20:09,030
No livestock allowed inside.

543
00:20:09,030 --> 00:20:10,110
No livestock allowed inside.

544
00:20:10,110 --> 00:20:10,960
No, this is...

545
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:14,070
This is not livestock.

546
00:20:14,070 --> 00:20:14,960
It's a pet.

547
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:17,480
My granddaughter doesn't want
to keep it anymore,

548
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:19,240
so she left it with me.

549
00:20:19,480 --> 00:20:20,400
Jia.

550
00:20:20,400 --> 00:20:21,070
Jia, come here.

551
00:20:21,070 --> 00:20:22,030
Help me get it out of here.

552
00:20:22,030 --> 00:20:22,830
Where is he?

553
00:20:23,960 --> 00:20:26,110
Just take a look.

554
00:20:26,110 --> 00:20:27,440
Look, it keeps spitting.

555
00:20:27,440 --> 00:20:29,110
How much effort could it take?

556
00:20:30,590 --> 00:20:32,310
Why are you so hardheaded?

557
00:20:32,310 --> 00:20:33,590
It's livestock.

558
00:20:33,920 --> 00:20:35,200
Go to a veterinary hospital.

559
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:36,350
Didn't I tell you?

560
00:20:36,350 --> 00:20:37,920
This is not livestock. It's a pet.

561
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:38,720
A pet?

562
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:40,120
Then go to a pet hospital.

563
00:20:40,200 --> 00:20:41,400
I did.

564
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:42,480
But they said

565
00:20:42,480 --> 00:20:43,830
they've never treated
anything like this before.

566
00:20:43,830 --> 00:20:44,350
Come on,

567
00:20:44,350 --> 00:20:45,550
you've got nothing else to do.

568
00:20:45,550 --> 00:20:46,480
Just take a look at it.

569
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:47,350
No.

570
00:20:47,350 --> 00:20:49,030
Look, it's spitting again.

571
00:20:49,030 --> 00:20:50,350
Is it sick?

572
00:20:50,350 --> 00:20:51,720
Sick?

573
00:20:51,720 --> 00:20:53,680
Sir, this...

574
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:54,790
I-It spits at people.

575
00:20:54,790 --> 00:20:55,880
That's...

576
00:20:55,880 --> 00:20:57,550
a normal reaction for it.

577
00:20:57,550 --> 00:20:59,270
It spits when it's scared

578
00:20:59,270 --> 00:20:59,960
or angry.

579
00:20:59,960 --> 00:21:01,000
It's not sick.

580
00:21:01,200 --> 00:21:01,960
Is it really not sick?

581
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:02,590
Nothing wrong.

582
00:21:02,590 --> 00:21:03,680
Nothing wrong at all.

583
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:04,790
Absolutely nothing wrong.

584
00:21:04,790 --> 00:21:05,480
That's good.

585
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:06,640
Look, I told you,

586
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:08,440
you can treat both humans and animals,

587
00:21:08,440 --> 00:21:09,000
right?

588
00:21:09,510 --> 00:21:10,550
Wasting so much time.

589
00:21:10,550 --> 00:21:10,790
Thank you.

590
00:21:10,790 --> 00:21:11,350
Alright.

591
00:21:11,350 --> 00:21:11,880
Hurry up and go.

592
00:21:11,880 --> 00:21:12,310
I'm leaving.

593
00:21:12,310 --> 00:21:13,030
You take it back

594
00:21:13,030 --> 00:21:15,160
and let it get used to the environment.

595
00:21:15,350 --> 00:21:16,270
Let's go.

596
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:17,200
Let's go.

597
00:21:17,200 --> 00:21:18,680
Let's go home.

598
00:21:19,610 --> 00:21:27,420
[Emergency]

599
00:21:22,480 --> 00:21:23,070
Granddaughter.

600
00:21:23,070 --> 00:21:24,270
I have good news for you.

601
00:21:24,270 --> 00:21:25,550
Dabao is fine.

602
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:27,270
It's not sick at all.

603
00:21:27,270 --> 00:21:28,310
Don't worry.

604
00:21:28,550 --> 00:21:29,310
While you're in Shanghai,

605
00:21:29,310 --> 00:21:30,550
work hard and focus on your job.

606
00:21:30,550 --> 00:21:32,310
Don't worry about things at home.

607
00:21:32,310 --> 00:21:33,400
I'm here to look after Dabao.

608
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:34,790
I know you're busy with work
and don't have time to take care of it.

609
00:21:34,790 --> 00:21:35,350
But don't worry,

610
00:21:35,350 --> 00:21:37,150
I'll take good care of it for you.

611
00:21:37,160 --> 00:21:37,690
Hurry up.

612
00:21:38,350 --> 00:21:39,550
Let's go home.

613
00:21:43,160 --> 00:21:44,620
The surgery was a success.

614
00:21:56,240 --> 00:21:57,750
Dr. Liu, Dr. Liu.

615
00:21:58,480 --> 00:21:59,310
Thank you so much.

616
00:21:59,310 --> 00:22:00,770
My mom is out of danger now.

617
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:01,960
Thank you.

618
00:22:01,960 --> 00:22:02,640
I wasn't sure

619
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:03,920
what to get you.

620
00:22:04,070 --> 00:22:04,960
Well,

621
00:22:04,960 --> 00:22:06,350
here, have this.

622
00:22:06,350 --> 00:22:07,350
What is it?

623
00:22:07,880 --> 00:22:08,590
Roasted sweet potato.

624
00:22:08,590 --> 00:22:09,790
It's freshly roasted and really sweet.

625
00:22:09,790 --> 00:22:11,030
Roasted sweet potato?

626
00:22:11,030 --> 00:22:11,560
It's hot.

627
00:22:13,070 --> 00:22:14,000
Great.

628
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:15,830
I've been constipated these past few days.

629
00:22:15,830 --> 00:22:16,880
Hospital policy says

630
00:22:16,880 --> 00:22:18,480
we can't accept gifts from patients.

631
00:22:18,480 --> 00:22:19,880
It's hardly a gift.

632
00:22:19,920 --> 00:22:22,050
It's just a sweet potato for you to eat.

633
00:22:22,110 --> 00:22:23,240
I'll take it for him.

634
00:22:23,960 --> 00:22:26,160
Our hospital doesn't have that policy.

635
00:22:26,880 --> 00:22:28,240
Take good care of your mom.

636
00:22:28,240 --> 00:22:29,970
She can eat and drink normally.

637
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:31,070
If she gets a fever,

638
00:22:31,070 --> 00:22:32,400
call a nurse right away.

639
00:22:32,750 --> 00:22:33,750
Tonight, I'll have Dr. Liu

640
00:22:33,750 --> 00:22:35,750
work overtime and keep an eye on her.

641
00:22:36,400 --> 00:22:37,720
That's wonderful. Thank you so much.

642
00:22:37,720 --> 00:22:38,640
Okay, okay!

643
00:22:38,640 --> 00:22:39,550
I won't keep you any longer.

644
00:22:39,550 --> 00:22:40,510
I'll go check on my mom.

645
00:22:40,510 --> 00:22:41,960
Bye-bye, Dr. Liu. See you tonight.

646
00:22:41,960 --> 00:22:43,490
Who said I'd work overtime?

647
00:22:43,590 --> 00:22:44,990
I'll treat you to dinner.

648
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:45,550
No.

649
00:22:46,350 --> 00:22:47,920
We're not going to a restaurant.

650
00:22:47,920 --> 00:22:48,750
Let's just find somewhere to sit,

651
00:22:48,750 --> 00:22:50,880
order some takeout, just the two of us.

652
00:22:51,720 --> 00:22:52,920
Then I want barbecue,

653
00:22:52,960 --> 00:22:54,490
the kind you had yesterday.

654
00:22:54,960 --> 00:22:56,620
Let's just have some skewers.

655
00:22:58,720 --> 00:23:00,680
Then I'll have a bowl of cold noodles,

656
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:01,790
plus ten skewers.

657
00:23:01,790 --> 00:23:03,790
Make it 20. Pretty generous, right?

658
00:23:05,070 --> 00:23:05,640
Deal.

659
00:23:23,070 --> 00:23:24,110
I've known you for a few days now,

660
00:23:24,110 --> 00:23:26,640
and this is the first time
I've seen you smile.

661
00:23:32,110 --> 00:23:33,000
You're young,

662
00:23:34,350 --> 00:23:35,750
you should smile more often.

663
00:23:35,750 --> 00:23:37,680
Don't look so serious all day long.

664
00:23:37,790 --> 00:23:38,850
When you get older,

665
00:23:39,590 --> 00:23:40,720
you won't have
much expression on your face,

666
00:23:40,720 --> 00:23:42,580
and it'll be even harder to smile.

667
00:23:53,550 --> 00:23:54,400
Duan...

668
00:23:55,830 --> 00:23:57,240
used to be my neighbor.

669
00:23:58,310 --> 00:23:59,000
She became a workshop director

670
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:00,240
at such a young age.

671
00:24:00,550 --> 00:24:02,080
She did things decisively.

672
00:24:03,110 --> 00:24:05,030
She had more backbone

673
00:24:05,590 --> 00:24:07,050
than many grown men I knew.

674
00:24:08,350 --> 00:24:09,880
She took good care of us too.

675
00:24:10,790 --> 00:24:12,960
Even now, people
still speak highly of her,

676
00:24:12,960 --> 00:24:13,760
including me.

677
00:24:18,440 --> 00:24:20,640
It's a pity. The paper mill was rebuilt,

678
00:24:21,070 --> 00:24:22,880
and over a hundred workers were laid off.

679
00:24:22,880 --> 00:24:24,880
The principles she'd lived by all her life

680
00:24:24,880 --> 00:24:26,610
suddenly didn't work anymore.

681
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:28,000
Her life

682
00:24:28,720 --> 00:24:30,160
got stuck in 1998.

683
00:24:41,030 --> 00:24:42,630
You came back from Shenzhen,

684
00:24:44,270 --> 00:24:46,530
so you must feel that contrast even more.

685
00:24:47,310 --> 00:24:50,110
The world outside is changing every day.

686
00:24:51,720 --> 00:24:53,030
But our city

687
00:24:53,680 --> 00:24:55,350
is getting older and older.

688
00:24:56,830 --> 00:24:59,030
Just like the older people around here,

689
00:24:59,720 --> 00:25:00,440
their way of thinking

690
00:25:00,440 --> 00:25:01,920
is stuck in the year 2000.

691
00:25:08,270 --> 00:25:10,070
What does that have to do with me?

692
00:25:10,350 --> 00:25:11,480
Isn't your family from here?

693
00:25:11,480 --> 00:25:13,680
No, I'm from Shenzhen.

694
00:25:16,440 --> 00:25:18,100
Quit putting on an act with me.

695
00:25:22,400 --> 00:25:24,000
You're done eating already?

696
00:25:24,440 --> 00:25:25,900
What about those skewers?

697
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:27,640
I'm full.

698
00:25:28,270 --> 00:25:28,920
Leave them for those

699
00:25:28,920 --> 00:25:30,980
colleagues working the night shift.

700
00:25:31,590 --> 00:25:33,920
Roasted sweet potato. Don't you want one?

701
00:25:45,920 --> 00:25:46,830
What a waste.

702
00:25:48,960 --> 00:25:51,160
Playing the sympathy card didn't work.

703
00:25:53,900 --> 00:26:00,660
[Xiaoximen Hospital,
the guardian of your health]

704
00:26:11,120 --> 00:26:15,870
[Emergency]

705
00:27:09,200 --> 00:27:10,030
You're awake.

706
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:13,330
Why are you so careless?

707
00:27:13,720 --> 00:27:15,650
Don't you know your own condition?

708
00:27:19,240 --> 00:27:20,720
You silly child,

709
00:27:21,270 --> 00:27:23,130
making me feel worried every day.

710
00:27:29,680 --> 00:27:30,480
Come here.

711
00:27:37,640 --> 00:27:38,970
It's okay, Zhengliang.

712
00:27:39,030 --> 00:27:39,960
Mom is here.

713
00:27:40,160 --> 00:27:42,070
It's okay, son. It's okay.

714
00:27:44,510 --> 00:27:46,200
I'll make you some dumplings.

715
00:27:46,310 --> 00:27:47,000
Okay?

716
00:28:06,680 --> 00:28:07,720
What was that?

717
00:28:08,240 --> 00:28:10,240
I borrowed it from the kid next door.

718
00:28:14,200 --> 00:28:16,200
Who brought me here yesterday?

719
00:28:16,440 --> 00:28:17,240
Uncle Dong.

720
00:28:18,200 --> 00:28:19,750
Uncle Dong? Who is that?

721
00:28:20,310 --> 00:28:21,240
The president.

722
00:28:21,480 --> 00:28:22,790
His full name is Long Dongdong.

723
00:28:22,790 --> 00:28:23,850
You don't know him?

724
00:28:24,110 --> 00:28:25,680
What a funny name.

725
00:28:26,240 --> 00:28:27,110
Since when did you

726
00:28:27,110 --> 00:28:28,510
become a relative of his?

727
00:28:29,270 --> 00:28:30,200
Liu Zhengliang.

728
00:28:30,350 --> 00:28:31,070
At first,

729
00:28:31,110 --> 00:28:32,470
I thought you'd recovered a long time ago.

730
00:28:32,470 --> 00:28:34,000
I thought you were rushing back

731
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:35,860
because you hated the Northeast.

732
00:28:35,880 --> 00:28:37,790
So it turns out you're still sick?

733
00:28:38,480 --> 00:28:39,680
Forget about Mom's situation.

734
00:28:39,680 --> 00:28:40,310
Leave it to me.

735
00:28:40,310 --> 00:28:41,550
Just peacefully

736
00:28:41,590 --> 00:28:43,190
get your ass back down South.

737
00:28:44,240 --> 00:28:45,510
I'd like to leave,

738
00:28:45,880 --> 00:28:47,240
but can I?

739
00:28:47,270 --> 00:28:49,000
I'll talk to Uncle Dong for you.

740
00:28:50,350 --> 00:28:51,200
No need.

741
00:28:51,790 --> 00:28:52,720
I'll handle

742
00:28:52,750 --> 00:28:54,080
my own business myself.

743
00:28:55,400 --> 00:28:56,240
Hello,

744
00:28:56,270 --> 00:28:57,680
everybody!

745
00:28:56,880 --> 00:28:58,280
[AC is On; Please keep the door closed]

746
00:28:58,310 --> 00:28:58,660
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

747
00:28:59,680 --> 00:29:00,750
Get well soon.

748
00:29:01,110 --> 00:29:01,840
Smells good?

749
00:29:03,200 --> 00:29:04,530
Why did you buy flowers?

750
00:29:04,960 --> 00:29:07,830
Well, staying in the hospital for a day
is still a hospital stay.

751
00:29:07,830 --> 00:29:09,550
I couldn't show up empty-handed.

752
00:29:09,550 --> 00:29:10,160
Right?

753
00:29:11,160 --> 00:29:12,400
Hold on, Junnan.

754
00:29:12,720 --> 00:29:13,750
When you visited me a couple of days ago,

755
00:29:13,750 --> 00:29:14,590
you came empty-handed.

756
00:29:14,590 --> 00:29:15,750
He's only been here for one day,

757
00:29:15,750 --> 00:29:17,070
and I had a craniotomy.

758
00:29:17,110 --> 00:29:20,000
The difference in
how we're being treated is insane!

759
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:20,880
Are you seriously comparing my bond

760
00:29:20,880 --> 00:29:22,920
with you to my bond with your brother?

761
00:29:22,920 --> 00:29:23,680
When he and I

762
00:29:23,680 --> 00:29:24,640
were making mud pies and peeing

763
00:29:24,640 --> 00:29:25,480
by the roadside together as kids,

764
00:29:25,480 --> 00:29:26,880
what were you doing then?

765
00:29:27,310 --> 00:29:28,970
You were still a nursing baby!

766
00:29:40,590 --> 00:29:42,110
I shouldn't have brought this up.

767
00:29:42,110 --> 00:29:43,350
I miss my mom.

768
00:29:46,550 --> 00:29:48,070
Now you've made me sad.

769
00:29:48,550 --> 00:29:50,080
I shouldn't have said that.

770
00:29:50,720 --> 00:29:51,830
Don't take it to heart.

771
00:29:51,830 --> 00:29:52,560
Give me a hug.

772
00:29:54,480 --> 00:29:55,510
Alright, leave him alone.

773
00:29:55,510 --> 00:29:56,910
He'll be fine in a minute.

774
00:29:59,960 --> 00:30:00,640
Uncle Dong.

775
00:30:00,720 --> 00:30:01,380
Uncle Dong.

776
00:30:02,480 --> 00:30:03,480
Everyone's here.

777
00:30:05,070 --> 00:30:06,200
How are you feeling?

778
00:30:08,510 --> 00:30:10,440
Can we talk privately for a moment?

779
00:30:12,000 --> 00:30:12,640
Sure.

780
00:30:13,270 --> 00:30:14,670
Come downstairs with me.

781
00:30:19,430 --> 00:30:23,220
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

782
00:30:32,070 --> 00:30:33,240
Don't worry.

783
00:30:33,480 --> 00:30:34,790
I'll pay you back

784
00:30:34,880 --> 00:30:36,070
for last night's hospital stay.

785
00:30:36,070 --> 00:30:37,270
Just go to the cashier window

786
00:30:37,270 --> 00:30:38,730
and pay it there yourself.

787
00:30:45,000 --> 00:30:45,750
When you have time,

788
00:30:45,750 --> 00:30:46,920
stop by my office to

789
00:30:51,830 --> 00:30:54,290
finish the paperwork for your resignation.

790
00:30:57,160 --> 00:30:59,480
When you told me
about your illness before,

791
00:30:59,480 --> 00:31:00,720
I was a bit skeptical.

792
00:31:01,830 --> 00:31:03,890
I didn't realize it was this serious.

793
00:31:05,070 --> 00:31:07,530
I never make things
difficult for patients.

794
00:31:09,000 --> 00:31:11,730
And the Northeast really
isn't the place for you.

795
00:31:15,270 --> 00:31:17,470
You're free to leave whenever you want.

796
00:31:24,160 --> 00:31:24,960
That's all.

797
00:31:43,160 --> 00:31:44,720
Sir, just pull over to the right.

798
00:31:44,030 --> 00:31:48,290
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

799
00:31:44,720 --> 00:31:46,000
Did you see that man waving?

800
00:31:46,000 --> 00:31:46,550
Right.

801
00:31:49,480 --> 00:31:50,070
Okay.

802
00:31:50,200 --> 00:31:50,830
There you are, sis.

803
00:31:50,830 --> 00:31:51,360
Hey, man.

804
00:31:51,590 --> 00:31:52,480
Hello, ma'am.

805
00:31:53,110 --> 00:31:54,070
-Mom, careful.
-Sis.

806
00:31:54,070 --> 00:31:54,310
Go ahead.

807
00:31:54,310 --> 00:31:55,440
This is the last place we're looking at.

808
00:31:54,570 --> 00:31:58,870
[Fucheng City Taxi]

809
00:31:55,480 --> 00:31:56,720
But I'll be honest with you.

810
00:31:56,720 --> 00:31:57,030
I won't give you

811
00:31:57,030 --> 00:31:58,030
the runaround.

812
00:31:58,160 --> 00:31:58,920
This one

813
00:31:58,920 --> 00:31:59,830
really isn't as good as the two places

814
00:31:59,830 --> 00:32:00,720
we looked at near the No. 1 Hospital.

815
00:32:00,720 --> 00:32:01,510
How so?

816
00:32:01,550 --> 00:32:02,270
Look across the street.

817
00:32:02,270 --> 00:32:03,480
Isn't that Xiaoximen Hospital?

818
00:32:03,480 --> 00:32:04,240
There are fewer patients there.

819
00:32:04,240 --> 00:32:05,640
Fewer patients means less business.

820
00:32:05,640 --> 00:32:06,550
The two places near the No. 1 Hospital

821
00:32:06,550 --> 00:32:07,200
are much more sought-after.

822
00:32:07,200 --> 00:32:09,330
No one has even asked about this place.

823
00:32:09,510 --> 00:32:10,640
What about the rent?

824
00:32:11,350 --> 00:32:12,830
If you're on a tight budget,

825
00:32:12,830 --> 00:32:13,720
this place will do.

826
00:32:13,720 --> 00:32:14,070
But, sis,

827
00:32:14,070 --> 00:32:15,550
you don't look like you're short on money.

828
00:32:15,550 --> 00:32:16,230
That's true.

829
00:32:16,230 --> 00:32:16,640
Right?

830
00:32:16,640 --> 00:32:17,440
That's true.

831
00:32:17,640 --> 00:32:18,750
Shall we take a look at this one?

832
00:32:18,750 --> 00:32:20,000
Go ahead. Open it.

833
00:32:20,240 --> 00:32:21,030
Sure.

834
00:32:21,440 --> 00:32:23,440
This used to be a noodle shop, right?

835
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:30,830
How long

836
00:32:30,830 --> 00:32:32,270
has this place been empty?

837
00:32:32,270 --> 00:32:33,130
Almost a month.

838
00:32:33,310 --> 00:32:34,270
The previous noodle shop

839
00:32:34,270 --> 00:32:35,200
closed down suddenly.

840
00:32:35,200 --> 00:32:36,330
They left in a hurry.

841
00:32:36,440 --> 00:32:38,000
Why did they close up the shop?

842
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:39,200
Someone in the family got sick.

843
00:32:39,200 --> 00:32:40,510
The couple went back to their hometown.

844
00:32:39,530 --> 00:32:42,990
[Fucheng City Food Business
Operator Information Disclosure Board]

845
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:43,530
There's a decent amount
of foot traffic here.

846
00:32:46,510 --> 00:32:48,240
There's nothing you can do
about life and death.

847
00:32:48,240 --> 00:32:51,040
-Ai Chen.
-This place gets good light, right, sis?

848
00:32:51,350 --> 00:32:54,010
It's nice that this bedroom
gets a little light.

849
00:32:55,590 --> 00:32:56,750
I want to cross the street

850
00:32:56,750 --> 00:32:58,200
to see Zhengguang.

851
00:32:58,680 --> 00:32:59,790
Come on.

852
00:33:00,400 --> 00:33:02,200
You're bored again, aren't you?

853
00:33:02,510 --> 00:33:03,590
You know

854
00:33:03,680 --> 00:33:05,590
I'm not interested in your business.

855
00:33:05,590 --> 00:33:07,350
Of course I know.

856
00:33:07,350 --> 00:33:08,240
Go ahead.

857
00:33:08,240 --> 00:33:09,440
I'll be fine on my own.

858
00:33:14,480 --> 00:33:15,310
The ceiling height in there...

859
00:33:15,310 --> 00:33:17,720
isn't it a bit low?

860
00:33:19,240 --> 00:33:20,700
You call this ceiling low?

861
00:33:21,160 --> 00:33:23,020
What exactly are you looking for?

862
00:33:23,240 --> 00:33:25,480
How do I pay the rent each month?

863
00:33:26,160 --> 00:33:27,200
What's the payment structure
for the rent and deposit?

864
00:33:27,200 --> 00:33:28,720
Is there a rent-free period?

865
00:33:28,720 --> 00:33:29,750
Sis, if money isn't an issue,

866
00:33:29,750 --> 00:33:30,480
you should rent one of those two places

867
00:33:30,480 --> 00:33:31,590
near the No. 1 Hospital.

868
00:33:31,590 --> 00:33:33,000
Here, the deposit is one month's rent,
and you have to pay three months upfront.

869
00:33:33,000 --> 00:33:33,680
There is no rent-free period.

870
00:33:33,680 --> 00:33:34,480
The price is non-negotiable.

871
00:33:34,480 --> 00:33:35,160
A rat!

872
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:36,590
Get lost.

873
00:33:41,000 --> 00:33:42,200
What's there to be afraid of?

874
00:33:42,200 --> 00:33:43,000
Well,

875
00:33:43,510 --> 00:33:45,170
I'm just scared of that thing.

876
00:33:45,550 --> 00:33:46,350
Hurry up.

877
00:33:46,750 --> 00:33:48,680
How much is the rent here, exactly?

878
00:34:01,030 --> 00:34:02,360
When are you going back?

879
00:34:04,750 --> 00:34:06,030
I'll buy a ticket as soon as I get home.

880
00:34:06,030 --> 00:34:07,510
I'll take whatever flight I can get.

881
00:34:07,510 --> 00:34:08,840
The sooner, the better.

882
00:34:10,880 --> 00:34:12,409
Do you have money to go back?

883
00:34:24,920 --> 00:34:25,710
Well,

884
00:34:26,070 --> 00:34:27,030
after paying your medical bills

885
00:34:27,030 --> 00:34:28,190
out of Mom's savings,

886
00:34:28,190 --> 00:34:29,230
there was a little left over.

887
00:34:29,230 --> 00:34:30,830
I'll use what's left for now.

888
00:34:31,110 --> 00:34:32,750
Once I'm back on my feet financially,

889
00:34:32,750 --> 00:34:33,750
I'll pay you back.

890
00:34:33,920 --> 00:34:34,710
No need.

891
00:34:35,360 --> 00:34:36,889
You have your share anyway.

892
00:34:37,800 --> 00:34:38,840
You little brat.

893
00:34:39,880 --> 00:34:40,760
Didn't you say

894
00:34:40,760 --> 00:34:42,690
I wasn't worthy of being Mom's son?

895
00:34:45,760 --> 00:34:47,150
I knew you're petty!

896
00:34:47,710 --> 00:34:48,550
I made one comment,

897
00:34:48,550 --> 00:34:50,679
and you'll hold it against me for life.

898
00:34:53,400 --> 00:34:54,070
Aunt Mi?

899
00:34:55,190 --> 00:34:56,000
Zhengguang.

900
00:34:56,070 --> 00:34:56,880
No way.

901
00:34:58,760 --> 00:34:59,920
When did you get out?

902
00:34:59,920 --> 00:35:01,380
The day before yesterday.

903
00:35:01,920 --> 00:35:02,880
I went to the police station yesterday

904
00:35:02,880 --> 00:35:03,800
to sort something out.

905
00:35:03,800 --> 00:35:04,590
Otherwise,

906
00:35:04,710 --> 00:35:06,570
I would've come to see you sooner.

907
00:35:08,280 --> 00:35:11,000
I've heard your mom's situation.

908
00:35:12,440 --> 00:35:13,970
Haven't they found her yet?

909
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:15,760
We still don't know what happened to her.

910
00:35:15,760 --> 00:35:16,890
When you get better,

911
00:35:16,920 --> 00:35:18,030
I'll go look for her with you.

912
00:35:18,030 --> 00:35:18,840
Okay.

913
00:35:19,280 --> 00:35:20,590
Liu Zhengguang, I'm leaving.

914
00:35:20,150 --> 00:35:25,350
[Non-Smoking Ward]

915
00:35:21,320 --> 00:35:22,180
It's Aunt Mi Si.

916
00:35:22,510 --> 00:35:24,110
She's a good friend of Mom's.

917
00:35:27,480 --> 00:35:29,510
That's my older brother, Liu Zhengliang.

918
00:35:29,510 --> 00:35:31,370
He's arrogant and has no manners.

919
00:35:31,400 --> 00:35:32,660
Please don't mind him.

920
00:35:32,840 --> 00:35:34,840
I've heard your mother mention him.

921
00:35:35,030 --> 00:35:35,880
He's afraid of snow.

922
00:35:35,880 --> 00:35:36,710
Yes.

923
00:35:36,960 --> 00:35:39,560
He's going back to Shenzhen
in a couple of days.

924
00:35:39,630 --> 00:35:41,320
To me, that means he'll be gone for good.

925
00:35:41,320 --> 00:35:42,450
Just don't mind him.

926
00:35:42,710 --> 00:35:43,590
Are you doing well?

927
00:35:43,590 --> 00:35:44,320
Pretty good.

928
00:35:44,510 --> 00:35:45,150
Auntie.

929
00:35:45,710 --> 00:35:47,630
Why did you come to
visit me empty-handed, too?

930
00:35:47,630 --> 00:35:48,840
How's that possible?

931
00:35:58,000 --> 00:35:59,590
I'm not a kid anymore.

932
00:35:59,630 --> 00:36:01,490
If you don't like it, give it to me.

933
00:36:02,230 --> 00:36:03,030
I like it.

934
00:36:03,550 --> 00:36:04,880
It's nice to put it here.

935
00:36:06,360 --> 00:36:10,490
[Shop for Rent]

936
00:36:06,400 --> 00:36:08,440
Sis, you really don't like
any of these places?

937
00:36:08,440 --> 00:36:09,360
No rush.

938
00:36:09,480 --> 00:36:10,840
I'll go home and think it over.

939
00:36:10,840 --> 00:36:12,110
We exchanged numbers, didn't we?

940
00:36:12,110 --> 00:36:13,070
Then I'll wait for your call.

941
00:36:13,070 --> 00:36:13,920
Okay. Thanks, buddy.

942
00:36:13,920 --> 00:36:14,760
It's a hot property.

943
00:36:14,760 --> 00:36:15,550
I know.

944
00:36:21,790 --> 00:36:24,240
[107 Xiaoximen Hospital]
[553 Xiaoximen Hospital]

945
00:36:40,670 --> 00:36:41,510
Oh no.

946
00:36:41,510 --> 00:36:42,320
Oh no, no, no.

947
00:36:42,320 --> 00:36:43,710
Jiao!

948
00:36:44,030 --> 00:36:45,280
Girl?

949
00:36:45,670 --> 00:36:46,600
Come on. Come on.

950
00:36:47,070 --> 00:36:48,510
I didn't see them!

951
00:36:48,510 --> 00:36:49,400
My daughter!

952
00:36:49,480 --> 00:36:50,230
Let's get you to the hospital.

953
00:36:50,230 --> 00:36:50,880
My daughter!

954
00:36:50,880 --> 00:36:52,080
It's okay. It's okay.

955
00:36:52,320 --> 00:36:54,930
[107 Xiaoximen Hospital]

956
00:36:54,280 --> 00:36:55,110
Hang in there.

957
00:36:55,710 --> 00:36:56,360
Kid.

958
00:36:56,360 --> 00:36:57,000
Come on.

959
00:36:57,000 --> 00:36:58,550
Open the door! Hurry!

960
00:36:58,550 --> 00:36:59,320
Open it!

961
00:37:02,360 --> 00:37:03,440
Emergency! Emergency!

962
00:37:03,440 --> 00:37:04,100
Go that way!

963
00:37:16,230 --> 00:37:17,960
I heard you couldn't open this door.

964
00:37:17,960 --> 00:37:19,510
Dr. Che insisted I get the door fixed.

965
00:37:19,510 --> 00:37:20,280
No need.

966
00:37:20,320 --> 00:37:21,110
Look.

967
00:37:21,150 --> 00:37:21,960
Dr. Liu.

968
00:37:22,150 --> 00:37:23,150
I heard from the president

969
00:37:23,150 --> 00:37:24,480
that you're resigning.

970
00:37:25,070 --> 00:37:27,600
I'm going upstairs
to sign the paperwork now.

971
00:37:27,630 --> 00:37:29,590
Why are you leaving
without saying anything?

972
00:37:29,590 --> 00:37:31,480
There was no need. We're not close.

973
00:37:31,480 --> 00:37:32,880
Dr. Che, we have a patient
from a car accident.

974
00:37:32,880 --> 00:37:33,840
Please go take a look.

975
00:37:33,840 --> 00:37:34,630
Coming.

976
00:37:38,440 --> 00:37:39,630
Go inside!

977
00:37:39,630 --> 00:37:40,110
Doctor!

978
00:37:40,110 --> 00:37:40,800
Is there a stretcher?

979
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:42,600
-Doctor!
-Is there a stretcher?

980
00:37:42,630 --> 00:37:43,760
Get a stretcher! Get a stretcher!

981
00:37:43,760 --> 00:37:44,800
Doctor.

982
00:37:45,150 --> 00:37:46,070
What happened?

983
00:37:46,630 --> 00:37:47,710
She was hit by a car.

984
00:37:48,510 --> 00:37:49,280
She got run over by a car.

985
00:37:49,280 --> 00:37:49,880
Jiao.

986
00:37:51,000 --> 00:37:53,280
-Slow down.
-My Jiao.

987
00:37:53,960 --> 00:37:55,510
Slow down.

988
00:37:56,190 --> 00:37:57,000
Let's go.

989
00:37:56,700 --> 00:37:57,780
[Chest Pain is Preferenced]

990
00:37:57,880 --> 00:37:58,670
Jiao.

991
00:37:59,360 --> 00:38:00,190
Careful.

992
00:38:02,840 --> 00:38:03,480
Huang.

993
00:38:03,480 --> 00:38:04,960
What's wrong with him?

994
00:38:05,070 --> 00:38:06,110
He faints at the sight of blood.

995
00:38:06,110 --> 00:38:07,630
He faints at the sight of blood?

996
00:38:07,630 --> 00:38:09,630
What kind of doctor faints at blood?

997
00:38:11,510 --> 00:38:12,230
Let me in.

998
00:38:12,920 --> 00:38:14,550
Get the patient's family out of the room.

999
00:38:14,550 --> 00:38:15,630
Come on, ma'am.

1000
00:38:15,630 --> 00:38:16,630
Ma'am, come here.

1001
00:38:19,960 --> 00:38:21,490
Let's wait outside for now.

1002
00:38:35,440 --> 00:38:36,440
We're trying to resuscitate the child.

1003
00:38:36,440 --> 00:38:37,110
We need to cut her clothes off.

1004
00:38:37,110 --> 00:38:38,310
Is that okay with you?

1005
00:38:38,440 --> 00:38:39,440
Yes, that's fine.

1006
00:38:43,510 --> 00:38:44,280
Zhang Jiao.

1007
00:38:44,510 --> 00:38:45,280
Zhang Jiao.

1008
00:38:50,630 --> 00:38:52,110
Laceration of the left temporal scalp

1009
00:38:52,110 --> 00:38:53,240
with exposed skull.

1010
00:38:53,590 --> 00:38:55,390
Severe bleeding from the wound.

1011
00:38:55,400 --> 00:38:57,660
Suspected open traumatic brain injury.

1012
00:38:59,130 --> 00:39:02,580
[Priority Care for Acute Stroke]

1013
00:39:01,440 --> 00:39:02,970
Fracture of the left thigh.

1014
00:39:03,480 --> 00:39:05,010
Abrasions on the lower leg.

1015
00:39:06,800 --> 00:39:07,880
Blood pressure is 60 over 40.

1016
00:39:07,880 --> 00:39:09,150
Heart rate is 154 beats per minute.

1017
00:39:09,150 --> 00:39:10,350
Establish IV access.

1018
00:39:10,400 --> 00:39:11,480
Give fluids to raise her blood pressure,

1019
00:39:11,480 --> 00:39:12,340
vasopressors,

1020
00:39:12,400 --> 00:39:13,760
100 mg dopamine,

1021
00:39:14,480 --> 00:39:15,480
250 mL saline,

1022
00:39:15,480 --> 00:39:16,140
and IV drip.

1023
00:39:16,150 --> 00:39:16,710
Got it.

1024
00:39:17,230 --> 00:39:18,030
Monitor her blood pressure.

1025
00:39:18,030 --> 00:39:18,590
Prepare mannitol.

1026
00:39:18,590 --> 00:39:19,960
You all saw what happened.

1027
00:39:19,960 --> 00:39:22,110
They fell onto the road first.

1028
00:39:22,440 --> 00:39:23,440
Stop talking.

1029
00:39:24,000 --> 00:39:24,590
Can't you see

1030
00:39:24,590 --> 00:39:25,510
what condition the child is in?

1031
00:39:25,510 --> 00:39:26,840
Ma'am, please make way.

1032
00:39:28,150 --> 00:39:28,810
This is bad.

1033
00:39:29,280 --> 00:39:30,740
Her left pupil is dilated.

1034
00:39:32,150 --> 00:39:33,840
Could this be brain herniation?

1035
00:39:33,840 --> 00:39:34,590
Her oxygen saturation is 85%.

1036
00:39:34,590 --> 00:39:35,670
And it's still dropping.

1037
00:39:35,670 --> 00:39:36,530
I'll take over.

1038
00:39:37,630 --> 00:39:38,290
Zhang Jiao.

1039
00:39:43,840 --> 00:39:45,320
She's going into respiratory failure.

1040
00:39:45,320 --> 00:39:46,280
Call Anesthesiology.

1041
00:39:46,280 --> 00:39:47,680
Prepare for intubation.

1042
00:39:47,710 --> 00:39:49,040
Put her on a ventilator.

1043
00:39:54,800 --> 00:39:55,590
Flashlight.

1044
00:39:57,000 --> 00:39:58,130
No, there's no time.

1045
00:39:58,150 --> 00:39:59,880
It'll take time
for the anesthesiology team to get here.

1046
00:39:59,880 --> 00:40:00,840
Brain herniation is extremely dangerous.

1047
00:40:00,840 --> 00:40:02,480
Her condition could deteriorate rapidly.

1048
00:40:02,480 --> 00:40:03,710
The patient is already showing

1049
00:40:03,710 --> 00:40:05,110
signs of respiratory failure.

1050
00:40:05,110 --> 00:40:06,510
If we don't act quickly,

1051
00:40:06,710 --> 00:40:08,110
she could die at any moment.

1052
00:40:08,110 --> 00:40:08,550
We must

1053
00:40:08,550 --> 00:40:09,710
get a CT scan immediately

1054
00:40:09,710 --> 00:40:11,360
to see what's happening in her brain.

1055
00:40:11,360 --> 00:40:12,480
Get me a bag-valve mask, now!

1056
00:40:12,480 --> 00:40:13,190
Here, here.

1057
00:40:13,320 --> 00:40:14,110
Move her to the CT room

1058
00:40:14,110 --> 00:40:14,880
for a scan.

1059
00:40:17,630 --> 00:40:18,440
Are you ready?

1060
00:40:18,440 --> 00:40:18,840
Ready.

1061
00:40:21,030 --> 00:40:22,360
Ma'am, please make way.

1062
00:40:24,660 --> 00:40:29,650
[Medication Pick-up]
[Prescription Review]

1063
00:40:29,910 --> 00:40:37,420
[Please keep the room clean]

1064
00:40:47,160 --> 00:40:50,340
[Please keep the room clean]

1065
00:40:55,800 --> 00:40:56,800
Mom, what's up?

1066
00:40:57,280 --> 00:40:58,880
Are you still house hunting?

1067
00:40:58,960 --> 00:41:00,110
No, I've stopped looking.

1068
00:41:00,110 --> 00:41:01,880
I'm on the first floor in the ER.

1069
00:41:01,920 --> 00:41:03,110
Something awful just happened.

1070
00:41:03,110 --> 00:41:05,770
I walked outside
and came across a car accident.

1071
00:41:05,800 --> 00:41:07,320
That girl was hit so badly,

1072
00:41:07,320 --> 00:41:09,280
I thought her brains were coming out.

1073
00:41:09,280 --> 00:41:10,940
I carried her to the hospital.

1074
00:41:13,230 --> 00:41:14,630
Can they save her?

1075
00:41:15,510 --> 00:41:17,030
I don't think she has much of a chance.

1076
00:41:17,030 --> 00:41:18,230
How can they save her?

1077
00:41:20,880 --> 00:41:22,760
Multiple fractures
of the left side of the skull,

1078
00:41:22,760 --> 00:41:24,880
extensive cerebral contusions
and lacerations

1079
00:41:24,880 --> 00:41:27,030
with subdural and intracerebral hematomas.

1080
00:41:27,030 --> 00:41:28,030
An estimated

1081
00:41:28,030 --> 00:41:29,710
blood volume of over 90 mL.

1082
00:41:30,190 --> 00:41:32,050
And the midline shift is over 2 cm.

1083
00:41:34,000 --> 00:41:35,060
Brain herniation.

1084
00:41:36,760 --> 00:41:37,920
There's no hope.

1085
00:41:38,590 --> 00:41:39,800
Notify the family.

1086
00:41:41,400 --> 00:41:43,110
Surgery might still save her.

1087
00:41:44,630 --> 00:41:45,480
Look at the scan—

1088
00:41:45,480 --> 00:41:46,760
her brain's severely damaged.

1089
00:41:46,760 --> 00:41:48,360
It looks like crumbled tofu.

1090
00:41:48,590 --> 00:41:51,320
How can we save her
if her brain has been shattered like this?

1091
00:41:51,320 --> 00:41:51,590
That means without surgery,

1092
00:41:51,590 --> 00:41:53,250
she'll almost certainly die.

1093
00:41:53,280 --> 00:41:54,710
Surgery can give her
a slim chance of survival!

1094
00:41:54,710 --> 00:41:56,000
Easy for you to say.

1095
00:41:56,070 --> 00:41:57,590
Who at Xiaoximen Hospital
could perform this surgery?

1096
00:41:57,590 --> 00:41:58,880
Even Director Tong couldn't do it,

1097
00:41:58,880 --> 00:42:00,110
let alone us.

1098
00:42:00,110 --> 00:42:01,150
Can you do it, can I do it,

1099
00:42:01,150 --> 00:42:01,960
or can Dr. Yang do it?

1100
00:42:01,960 --> 00:42:02,670
He can!

1101
00:42:05,180 --> 00:42:12,440
[Priority Care for Acute Stroke]

1102
00:42:09,150 --> 00:42:09,960
Dr. Liu.

1103
00:42:11,030 --> 00:42:12,030
I saw you

1104
00:42:12,030 --> 00:42:14,160
operate on your brother the other day.

1105
00:42:14,480 --> 00:42:15,710
You're so skilled.

1106
00:42:16,150 --> 00:42:17,590
Can you save this child?

1107
00:42:19,280 --> 00:42:20,800
Given her condition,

1108
00:42:20,960 --> 00:42:23,020
the surgery is extremely difficult.

1109
00:42:24,110 --> 00:42:26,110
Even if my mentor performed the surgery,

1110
00:42:26,110 --> 00:42:27,840
he might not be able to save her.

1111
00:42:33,510 --> 00:42:34,320
Then...

1112
00:42:35,400 --> 00:42:36,110
we can't just

1113
00:42:36,110 --> 00:42:36,960
stand by and watch

1114
00:42:36,960 --> 00:42:38,190
her die, can we?

1115
00:42:41,360 --> 00:42:42,030
Enough.

1116
00:42:42,190 --> 00:42:43,790
Don't put Dr. Liu on the spot.

1117
00:42:43,840 --> 00:42:45,440
He doesn't even work here anymore.

1118
00:42:45,440 --> 00:42:47,640
Why are you dragging him into this mess?

1119
00:42:52,230 --> 00:42:53,550
Are you afraid her family will

1120
00:42:53,550 --> 00:42:55,070
cause trouble if you fail to save her?

1121
00:42:55,070 --> 00:42:56,000
I'll go talk to them.

1122
00:42:56,000 --> 00:42:58,060
You just need to focus on the surgery.

1123
00:42:58,360 --> 00:42:59,550
Let's take a gamble,

1124
00:42:59,840 --> 00:43:00,630
okay?

1125
00:43:12,360 --> 00:43:13,110
I can't take that risk.
